UID:alkazi-curatorial-research-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
SUMMARY:Deadline: Alkazi Foundation: Curatorial Research Fellowship 2027 (w
 ith CWIT and the V&A)
DESCRIPTION:A funded research residency (3rd edition of the Visiting Curato
 rial Research Fellowship) for mid-career cultural producers from India: ar
 tists\, scholars\, writers/editors and curators pursuing humanities-driven
  research in the V&A's global photography and visual-culture collections i
 n London. The awardee is announced in February 2027 and the fellowship sta
 rts April 2027. SUPPORT: GBP 1\,600 per month\, GBP 800 towards return air
 fare (CWIT) and visa costs covered. ELIGIBILITY: Indian citizens domiciled
  in India\, aged 25 to 45\, mid-career. APPLY by email to alkazifoundation
 01@gmail.com with subject 'Curatorial Research Fellowship 2027'. DEADLINE:
  7 November 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Alkazi Foundation for the Arts\, with t
 he Charles Wallace India Trust and the Victoria and Albert Museum\nLocatio
 n: New Delhi\, India (organiser)\; the funded research residency takes pla
 ce at the V&A Photography Section\, London. RESTRICTED: Indian citizens do
 miciled in India\, aged 25 to 45\, mid-career.\nAward: GBP 1\,600 monthly 
 stipend for 3 to 6 months\, plus a GBP 800 contribution from CWIT towards 
 international return airfare\; visa expenses covered by the Alkazi Foundat
 ion. No application fee.\nDuration: 3 to 6 months\n\nMore: https://alkazif
 oundation.org/call-for-entries-5/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
URL:https://alkazifoundation.org/call-for-entries-5/?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New Delhi\, India (organiser)\; the funded research residency take
 s place at the V&A Photography Section\, London. RESTRICTED: Indian citize
 ns domiciled in India\, aged 25 to 45\, mid-career.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tarbell-fellowship-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:Deadline: Tarbell Fellowship 2027-28 (AI journalism)
DESCRIPTION:A year-long fellowship for journalists covering artificial inte
 lligence. Fellows complete a three-month full-time remote programme on AI 
 and journalism fundamentals\, attend a weeklong summit\, then work for nin
 e months as reporters embedded in a partner newsroom (current partners are
  in Hong Kong\, London\, Los Angeles\, New York\, San Francisco\, Seattle\
 , Washington DC and Cambridge). ELIGIBILITY: journalism or AI expertise\, 
 aged 18+ by 7 June 2027\, no degree required\; primarily for applicants wi
 th the right to work in the US\, UK or Hong Kong\, as visa sponsorship is 
 uncommon and needs partner-outlet approval.\n\nOrganisation: Tarbell Cente
 r for AI Journalism\nLocation: Remote training\, then newsroom placement i
 n the US\, UK or Hong Kong. In person.\nAward: USD 75\,000 to 120\,000 dep
 ending on experience and placement cost of living\; senior fellows (7+ yea
 rs experience) USD 115\,000 to 135\,000. Summit travel and accommodation c
 overed. No application fee.\nDuration: 12 months: remote training 7 June t
 o 6 August 2027\, in-person summit August 2027\, newsroom placement Septem
 ber 2027 to May 2028 (extendable by one year).\n\nMore: https://www.tarbel
 lcenter.org/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://www.tarbellcenter.org/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote training\, then newsroom placement in the US\, UK or Hong K
 ong. In person.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mplus-sigg-fellowship-chinese-art-research-2026-27@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
SUMMARY:Deadline: M+ Sigg Fellowship for Chinese Art Research 2026/27 (HKD 
 200\,000\, Hong Kong)
DESCRIPTION:The Sigg Fellowship for Chinese Art Research supports new resea
 rch on Chinese art in dialogue with the M+ Collections\; the 2026/27 editi
 on focuses on tradition and contemporary Chinese art. WHO: individuals or 
 research groups of any nationality and any age\, with a postgraduate degre
 e in a relevant discipline\, or an undergraduate degree plus at least thre
 e years of relevant professional or academic research experience\; profici
 ency in spoken and written Chinese or English is required\, and the fellow
 ship is subject to obtaining a Hong Kong visa. WHAT YOU GET: HKD 200\,000 
 to cover all expenses\, including travel\, living\, insurance and research
  costs\, for a three-to-six-month attachment to M+. Fellows give a public 
 lecture in Hong Kong and write an essay of at least 5\,000 English words o
 r 7\,500 Chinese characters for M+ Magazine. APPLICATION: submit a researc
 h proposal (max 1\,000 words) and full CV via the Google form on the call 
 page\, in English or Chinese\, and have two academic or professional refer
 ees email recommendation letters directly. Results are announced in early 
 2027. DEADLINE: 30 November 2026\, 23:59 (UTC+8).\n\nOrganisation: M+\, We
 st Kowloon Cultural District\nLocation: Hong Kong. Open to individuals or 
 research groups of any nationality\; the fellowship depends on obtaining a
  Hong Kong visa.\nAward: HKD 200\,000 covering all expenses (travel\, livi
 ng\, insurance and research costs). No application fee mentioned.\nDuratio
 n: 3 to 6 months attached to M+ in Hong Kong.\n\nMore: https://www.mplus.o
 rg.hk/en/awards-and-fellowships/sigg-fellowship-for-chinese-art-research/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mplus.org.hk/en/awards-and-fellowships/sigg-fellowship-for-
 chinese-art-research/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
LOCATION:Hong Kong. Open to individuals or research groups of any nationali
 ty\; the fellowship depends on obtaining a Hong Kong visa.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:parc-palestinian-research-fellowship-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261205
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261206
SUMMARY:Deadline: PARC Palestinian Research Fellowship 2027-2028 (up to USD
  6\,000\, arts\, humanities and social sciences)
DESCRIPTION:PARC's 28th annual fellowship competition for Palestinian schol
 ars funds field-based research in the arts\, humanities\, social sciences\
 , public health and environmental studies\; purely scientific research is 
 not eligible. WHO: Palestinian PhD students who have defended their disser
 tation proposal\, or Palestinian PhD holders\, regardless of residence or 
 ID\; researchers without a doctorate qualify with at least 10 refereed art
 icles\, and MA holders only as part of a team led by a PhD holder. Recent 
 PARC fellows (last three years) are ineligible. FIELDWORK: in Palestine\, 
 Jordan\, Egypt or Lebanon\, lasting two months to one year (Golan Heights 
 proposals accepted with a comparative Palestine framework). WHAT YOU GET: 
 up to USD 6\,000\, with research to be completed by 31 December 2028. APPL
 ICATION: in English via the Apply Now link (application form\, 350-word ab
 stract\, 2\,000-word proposal\, service component\, budget\, CV up to 10 p
 ages\, ID and passport details\; PhD students also transcripts and two rec
 ommendation letters). Information webinar 27 October 2026\; awards announc
 ed 15 April 2027. DEADLINE: 5 December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Palestinian 
 American Research Center (PARC)\nLocation: For Palestinian researchers reg
 ardless of residence or ID\; fieldwork in Palestine\, Jordan\, Egypt or Le
 banon.\nAward: Up to USD 6\,000 per fellowship (tuition not covered). No a
 pplication fee mentioned.\nDuration: 2 to 12 months of fieldwork\; researc
 h to be completed by 31 December 2028.\n\nMore: https://www.parc-us-pal.or
 g/fellowships-for-palestinians/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
URL:https://www.parc-us-pal.org/fellowships-for-palestinians/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:For Palestinian researchers regardless of residence or ID\; fieldw
 ork in Palestine\, Jordan\, Egypt or Lebanon.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
